## Visual Design

No toggles. Everything meaningful is always visible.

| Element | Color / Style |
|---------|--------------|
| Background | White |
| Grid | Light grey |
| Lines, branches, components | Black |
| Auto-nodes (branch intersections) | Black dots |
| Defined nodes (N key) | Green dots |
| Supernode region | Pale blue filled rectangle behind area |
| Defined voltage segments (V key) | Pale pink filled rectangle behind area |
| Loop current arrows | Blue circular arrows, variable name centered inside |
| Passive value labels | Small grey text, always visible near named entity |

Loop current naming — default i_n (auto-incrementing: i_1, i_2...). Name is required before placement confirms. Press L, draw/select loop, prompt appears pre-filled with i_n default, confirm, arrow renders.

---

## Rendering

- Components render as classic circuit symbols (zigzag resistor, circle source, diamond dependent source, etc.)
- Symbols are visually placed within the bounding region defined by the branch they sit on.
- Node dots auto-appear where 3+ branches meet.
- Ground symbol available as a special terminal.

